Subject: [PATCH] assert.h: add ISO C11 static_assert macro

The existing features.h backport enables __USE_ISOC11 for C11 builds,
but uClibc 0.9.33.2's assert.h does not provide the C11 static_assert
macro.

GCC 7.5.0 supports the C11 _Static_assert keyword, so expose the
standard static_assert spelling from <assert.h> when ISO C11 features
are enabled.  Keep it disabled for C++ where static_assert is a
language keyword.

This mirrors the implementation used by glibc when C11 static
assertions were introduced.

---
 include/assert.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/include/assert.h
+++ b/include/assert.h
@@ -77,3 +77,9 @@
 # endif
 
 #endif /* NDEBUG.  */
+
+#if defined __USE_ISOC11 && !defined __cplusplus
+/* Static assertion.  Requires support in the compiler. */
+# undef static_assert
+# define static_assert _Static_assert
+#endif
-- 
